/-!
# The numerical type of a regular model

Let `R` be a local ring of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by a
nonzerodivisor `π`, for instance a discrete valuation ring with a uniformizer, with residue field
`k`, and let `X` be a regular Noetherian integral scheme, proper and flat over `R`, all of whose
points have codimension at most two, such as a proper regular model of a curve over `R`. Let
`Cᵢ` be the irreducible components of the special fibre, with their reduced structures; `H⁰` and
`H¹` of the structure sheaf of every `Cᵢ` are finite-dimensional over `k`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.finiteDimensional_cohomology_trivial_subscheme_closure_singleton`).

Following [Stacks, Section 55.9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Y), the special fibre
then defines a numerical type in the sense of
[Stacks, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z)
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType`), independent of the generator `π`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_congr`), with

* components the irreducible components `Cᵢ` of the special fibre;
* multiplicities `mᵢ`, the orders of vanishing of `π` along the `Cᵢ`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultiplicity`);
* weights `wᵢ = [κᵢ : k] = dim_k H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, where `κᵢ = H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` is the constant
  field of `Cᵢ` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeight`);
* genera `gᵢ = dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, taken over the constant field;
* intersection matrix `aᵢⱼ = (Cⱼ · Cᵢ)`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`).

The axioms of a numerical type are the properties of these data proved in
`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IntersectionNumber.Matrix` and
`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IntersectionNumber.Weight`: the intersection matrix is symmetric with
nonnegative off-diagonal entries and kills the multiplicity vector, its graph is connected
because the special fibre is
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isPreconnected_preimage_closedPoint_iff_reflTransGen`), and `wᵢ`
divides its `i`-th row. The component set is nonempty by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.nonempty_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint`.

The combinatorial theory of `TauCeti.NumericalType`, such as its signed genus
`TauCeti.NumericalType.arithmeticGenus` and its weighted Picard group
`TauCeti.NumericalType.Pic`, thereby applies to regular models.

## Main declarations

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType`: the numerical type of the special
  fibre of a regular model.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_weight`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_intersection` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_genus`: its data, and its independence of
  `π` proved in `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_congr`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus`:
  `wᵢ gᵢ = dim_k H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, comparing the genus over the constant field with the genus
  over the residue field.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_adj_iff`: two distinct components are
  adjacent exactly when they intersect.

## Implementation notes

The definition is exposed so that its component type is, definitionally, the type of
codimension-one points of `X` in the special fibre that indexes
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Section 55.3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Y),
  [Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z), and
  [Section 55.9 (Tag 0C5Y)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Y).
* Q. Liu, *Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Curves*, Section 9.1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing Order
open TauCeti TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData (vanishingIdeal)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R))

variable [Ring.DimensionLEOne R] [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X]
  [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X] [IsProper toBase] [Flat toBase]
  [ConnectedSpace (specialFiber R toBase).left]

/-- **The numerical type of a regular model**
([Stacks, Section 55.9 (Tag 0C5Y)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Y)). Let `X` be a
regular Noetherian integral scheme, proper and flat over a local ring `R` of dimension at most one
whose maximal ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor `π`, with connected special fibre and all
points of codimension at most two. Its numerical type
([Stacks, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z)) has the components of the special
fibre as its components, with

* multiplicity `mᵢ` the multiplicity of `Cᵢ` in the divisor of `π`,
* weight `wᵢ = [κᵢ : k]` the degree of the constant field `κᵢ = H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`,
* intersection matrix `aᵢⱼ = (Cⱼ · Cᵢ)`, and
* genus `gᵢ = dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, the arithmetic genus of `Cᵢ` over its constant field.

The definition is exposed so that the component type is definitionally the finite set of
codimension-one points of the special fibre indexing
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`. -/
@[expose]
def specialFiberNumericalType (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
    {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π) :
    NumericalType.{u} :=
  have hπm : π ∈ maximalIdeal R := hπ ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self π
  have hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R :=
    toBase.base_genericPoint_ne_closedPoint_of_isSMulRegular hπm hreg
  have hR : maximalIdeal R ≠ ⊥ := toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη
  have hπ0 : π ≠ 0 := toBase.ne_zero_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη hπ
  letI : DecidableEq (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint hR hη).toFinset := Classical.decEq _
  letI : Nonempty (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint hR hη).toFinset := by
    obtain ⟨η, hc⟩ := toBase.nonempty_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint hη
    exact ⟨⟨η, (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mpr hc⟩⟩
  { Component := (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint hR hη).toFinset
    multiplicity j := ⟨toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j,
      toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_pos hη hπm hπ0 j ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp j.property)⟩
    weight i := ⟨toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.property),
      toBase.specialFiberWeight_pos _
        (toBase.finiteDimensional_cohomology_trivial_subscheme_closure_singleton hX
          ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.property) 0)⟩
    intersection := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη
    intersection_isSymm := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_isSymm hX hη
    offDiagonal_nonneg _ _ hij := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_nonneg_of_ne hX hη hij
    connected := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_reflTransGen hX hη
      ((connectedSpace_specialFiber_iff_isPreconnected R toBase).mp inferInstance)
    fiber_relation i := by
      have h := congrFun
        (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_mulVec_specialFiberMultiplicity hX hη hπ hreg) i
      simpa [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, mul_comm] using h
    weight_dvd := toBase.specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη
    genus i := Module.finrank
      Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.val : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
      (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial (vanishingIdeal
        ⟨closure {(i.val : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) }

section Projections

variable (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
  {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π)

/-- The component type of `specialFiberNumericalType` is the finite subtype of codimension-one
points of `X` lying in the special fibre. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_Component (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).Component =
      ↥(toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset := (rfl)

/-- Every component of `specialFiberNumericalType` lies over the closed point of `Spec R`. -/
theorem base_eq_closedPoint_of_specialFiberNumericalType
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).Component) :
    toBase (i.val : X) = closedPoint R := (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.property

/-- The multiplicity of a component of the special fibre in the numerical type of a regular model
is the order of vanishing of `π` along it. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).Component) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).multiplicity i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i.val :=
  rfl

/-- The weight of a component `C` of the special fibre in the numerical type of a regular model is
`dim_k H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)`, the degree of the constant field of `C` over the residue field `k`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).Component) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).weight i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberWeight
        (toBase.base_eq_closedPoint_of_specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg i) :=
  rfl

/-- The intersection matrix of the numerical type of a regular model is the intersection matrix of
its special fibre. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_intersection :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).intersection =
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX
        (toBase.base_genericPoint_ne_closedPoint_of_isSMulRegular
          (hπ ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self π) hreg) :=
  rfl

/-- The `(i, j)`-entry of the intersection matrix of `specialFiberNumericalType`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_intersection_apply
    (i j : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).Component) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).intersection i j =
      letI := subschemeOverResidueField
        (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
          (toBase.base_eq_closedPoint_of_specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg i))
      LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber (ResidueField R)
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.val : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι
        (LineBundleClass.mk
          (Scheme.IdealSheafData.isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular
            hX j.val.property).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ :=
  toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_apply hX _ i j

/-- Two components are adjacent in the numerical type of a regular model exactly when they are
distinct and their closures meet. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_adj_iff
    (i j : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).Component) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).Adj i j ↔
      i ≠ j ∧ (closure {(i.val : X)} ∩ closure {(j.val : X)}).Nonempty :=
  (NumericalType.adj_iff
    (T := toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg) (i := i) (j := j)).trans
      (and_congr_right fun hij ↦ toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_pos_iff hX _ hij)

/-- The genus of a component `C` of the special fibre in the numerical type of a regular model is
`dim_{κ_C} H¹(C, 𝒪_C)`, over the ring `κ_C = H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)` of global functions on `C`, which is its
constant field. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_genus
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).Component) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).genus i = Module.finrank
      Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.val : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
      (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.val : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  rfl

/-- **Weight times genus is the genus over the residue field.** For a component `C` of the special
fibre of a regular model, with weight `w = [κ : k]` and genus `g = dim_κ H¹(C, 𝒪_C)` over its
constant field `κ` in the numerical type, `w g = dim_k H¹(C, 𝒪_C)` over the residue field `k`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).Component) :
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
      (toBase.base_eq_closedPoint_of_specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg i))
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).weight i : ℕ) *
        (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).genus i =
      Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.val : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  toBase.specialFiberWeight_mul_finrank_cohomology_one
    (toBase.base_eq_closedPoint_of_specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg i)

/-- **Uniformizer independence of `specialFiberNumericalType`.** Any two nonzerodivisor generators
of `maximalIdeal R` define the same `TauCeti.NumericalType`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_congr {π' : R}
    (hπ' : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π'}) (hreg' : IsSMulRegular R π') :
    toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg = toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ' hreg' :=
  let T := toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg
  (T.reindex_refl).symm.trans (T.reindex_eq (T' := toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ' hreg')
    (Equiv.refl T.Component)
    (fun i ↦ PNat.eq (toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_congr (hπ.symm.trans hπ') i.val).symm)
    (fun _ ↦ rfl) (fun _ _ ↦ rfl) fun _ ↦ rfl)

/-- The special fibre is reduced iff every component has multiplicity `1` in
`specialFiberNumericalType`. -/
theorem isReduced_specialFiber_iff_multiplicity_eq_one :
    IsReduced (specialFiber R toBase).left ↔
      ∀ i, (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hπ hreg).multiplicity i = 1 := by
  have hη := toBase.base_genericPoint_ne_closedPoint_of_isSMulRegular
    (hπ ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self π) hreg
  rw [toBase.isReduced_specialFiber_iff_specialFiberMultiplicity_eq_one_of_isRegular hX hη hπ]
  exact ⟨fun h i ↦ PNat.eq (h i.val ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.property)),
    fun h x hx ↦ congrArg PNat.val (h ⟨x, (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mpr hx⟩)⟩

end Projections

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

end
